A||||5||walsh2001||Gauge Swap?||||4||
Z||000000||walsh2001||09-04-2001||01:12 PM||||Is it common for the Fiero instrument cluster to short out? This seems to be my problem since the idiot lights, gas gauge, and temp gauge do not work. The Door Ajar light stays on as well. Any Ideas? (I have an 86 GT cluster to replace it with if necessary)||||reg||4
Z||000001||walsh2001||09-04-2001||01:17 PM||||Are the gauge sets fully interchangable between years... 86-87? Any calibration required?<P>------------------<BR>'87 Fiero GT ... Cherry Red||||reg||3
Z||000002||Wolfhound||09-04-2001||01:37 PM||||Jason, Check for corrosion  or looseness at the main connectors on the rear of the cluster. That's likely the problem.<BR>Yes, the 86GT-87GT clusters are interchangeable.<BR>No calibration required.<P>Another thought: When you turn the ignition to run, not start, do the effected guages jump to zero? <BR>Coy<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haagster||09-04-2001||01:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by walsh2001:<BR><B>Are the gauge sets fully interchangable between years... 86-87? Any calibration required?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's plug and pray.  [assuming everything works and you don't accidently loose one of the gauge needles in the transfer - been there] The "new" cluster just plugs in...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||09-04-2001||09:48 PM||||And if that happens throw the cluster up on the steering column without the clear faceplate. Plug it up.  Turn the ignition to run. Replace needle to Zero with a spot of super glue jell. Done ||||reg||1
Z||000005||walsh2001||09-05-2001||01:13 AM||||Thanks Wolfhound! I guess this will be tomorrow's project  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
